Chemical equilibria play important roles in various biological and environmental processes. Equilibria involving O2 molecules and the protein hemoglobin are involved in the transport and delivery of O2 from our lungs to our muscles. Evaporation of H2O (l) to H20 (g) i.e. leading to formation of cloud and simultaneous condensation of H2O (g) to H2O (l) leading to rain are common examples which we observe in our daily life. Other examples which involve H20 are;
H2O(s) ⇌H2O(l) ;
H2O (l) ⇌H2O(s)
